# KNOWN GAP (ASan lane). The value-lane twin is
# tests/fixtures/known_gaps/shared_vector_of_clones_unwritten_slot.gg — same program, different lane.
# SEGFAULTS (rc -11 / 139) reading an element that was never written.
#
# The Book Ch16 "many owners" idiom: several Shared handles to ONE value, held in
# a Vector. `all.len()` prints 3, so the container bookkeeping ran — only the
# PAYLOAD write is missing.
#
# Under `gg build --sanitize`, UBSan fires FIRST and names the cause:
#
#   runtime error: load of misaligned address 0xbebebebebebebebe
#                  for type 'int64_t', which requires 8 byte alignment
#   ERROR: AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address 0x17d7d7e7d7d7d7d7
#       #0 Shared__int64_t__get   #1 main
#
# 0xbe is ASan's UNINITIALISED-HEAP FILL, so the slot was never stored; the
# 0x17d7… address is that fill after the accessor's pointer arithmetic, one frame
# later. ⚠ Read the UBSan line before the ASan line — an earlier triage read only
# the SEGV and concluded the push and the read disagreed about LAYOUT, which
# points at the wrong fix.
#
# The self-host lane ALSO traps here, so there is no correct lane to use as an
# oracle for this one (unlike its sibling todo/t0108, where the self-host is
# right).
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired test): prints 3 then 42.
# Filed as todo/t0840. Found 2026-08-30 by R47 Track F4a, when the new verdict
# classifier stopped grading a signal death as `TRAP`.

void main():
    Shared[int] s = Shared[int](42)
    Vector[Shared[int]] all = []
    all.push(s.clone())
    all.push(s.clone())
    all.push(s.clone())
    print(f"{all.len()}")
    print(f"{all.get(1).unwrap().get()}")
